# Tauri — Vertical Slices

Host/domain logic lives in `src-tauri/src/slices/<slice>/`. This replaces an Electron main/preload process.

## Layout

```
src-tauri/src/
  lib.rs              # wiring only
  main.rs             # entry
  slices/
    <slice>/
      mod.rs          # public slice API
      commands.rs     # Tauri commands
```

## Rules

- `lib.rs` only wires plugins, state, and command registration
- No cross-slice domain logic in `lib.rs`
- Slices communicate through clear APIs, not internals
- Host/LAN serving is its own slice (e.g. `network`), not frontend code
- Frontend must call Tauri only through `@shared/api` facades

## Example

```rust
// lib.rs — wiring only
.invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![
    slices::greet::commands::greet,
])
```
